
"""
po_gantt_service.py  -  Production Schedule: PO on Process / PO on Machines / Planned vs Actual

    GET    /schedule/po-gantt                 the schedule (start_at = exact start, default now)
    GET    /schedule/po-gantt/orders          yet-to-start POs + part numbers of the plant (pickers; locked POs flagged)
    GET    /schedule/po-gantt/plants          plant codes
    GET    /schedule/po-gantt/process-check   every process: batch or series and why, batch size, machines
    GET    /schedule/po-gantt/export          the same schedule as .xlsx
    GET/PUT /schedule/part-process-time       machine hours + batch size per part / process
    GET/PUT /schedule/settings                every scheduling rule (Configure dialog) -> table schedule_settings
    POST   /schedule/plans                    save the schedule as a plan VERSION (new plan REV01 / revision REVnn)
    GET    /schedule/plans?plant=             saved versions with Plan_ID / Version_ID / Previous_Version_ID / reference
    GET    /schedule/plans/view               read-only Gantt data of a version for a date range (Assign PCB page)
    GET    /schedule/plans/{id}               one saved version with its snapshot
    PUT    /schedule/plans/{id}/baseline      make it the current plan of its plant
    DELETE /schedule/plans/{id}               only the newest version of a plan, and only if no PO was assigned from it
    GET    /schedule/plans/{id}/compare       planned (saved version) vs actual (operator_log / pcb_process_log)
    POST   /schedule/locks                    PCBs of these POs were assigned from a plan -> keep their slots
    GET    /schedule/locks?plant=             POs whose slots are kept
    DELETE /schedule/locks/{po}               release a PO's slots

Hook-up (Data_Server.py) - unchanged:
    from po_gantt_service import create_po_gantt_router
    app.include_router(create_po_gantt_router(init_db, verify_token, engine))

New tables (created automatically): schedule_settings, schedule_plan_version, schedule_po_lock.

RULES (every number / list / name below is a setting the user can change - see SETTINGS_SCHEMA)
 * POs come ONLY from PcbData. A PO is open when every one of its PCBs has a status in PCB_OPEN_STATUSES.
 * CHILD / MAIN: product_type_master, else PcbData.Type; main <- child link: same product type, else bom_items,
   else EXTRA_CHILD_LINKS. Child -> main POs by serial number first, then by quantity.
 * Flow of a part: product_workflow_mapping, else part_process_time in step order. LINE_GROUPS = steps run as one line.
 * Scheduling starts at the exact moment the schedule is made (or the start_at the user picks).
 * Working window per process: work centre (sap_workcenter_capacity) operating_time, else shift end - shift start minus
   the break; no work centre -> shift_definition; else the fallback settings. Nothing is rounded up to 2 shifts.
 * Machines from the work centre (number_of_individuals) / equipment_details; breakdowns, maintenance, spares and
   consumables block machines / processes; off days from the settings + public_holidays + calendar_exceptions.
 * A PO whose PCBs were assigned from a saved version keeps that version's slots (LOCK_ASSIGNED_SLOTS); later
   schedules are built around them.
"""
